questions.explanation:
**Given:**

\(\frac{1 - \cos 2\theta}{\sin 2\theta}\)

**Formula used:**

1 - cos 2&theta; = 2sin2&theta;

sin 2&theta; = 2sin&theta; cos&theta;

tan&theta; = sin&theta; / cos&theta;

**Calculation:**

\(\frac{1 - \cos 2\theta}{\sin 2\theta}\)

&rArr; \(\frac{2\sin^2\theta}{2\sin\theta \times \cos\theta}\)

&rArr; \(\frac{\sin\theta}{\cos\theta}\)

&rArr; tan&theta;

**&there4; The correct answer is option (4).**

